# Chroma library, modern Earth: SHAPE MOMENTS for the knowledge and career ladder shapes, v25 prep (draft, 10-23).
# The Library pours this into chroma-library/earth_shape_moments-*.lib (build.py earth_shape_moments); nothing reads it yet.
# Balance layout: five single ways and one full cross cycle per moment.
#   cycle s1: W>U U>B B>R R>G G>W      cycle s2: W>B B>G G>U U>R R>W      (13 moments each over the file)
# Slots: {aim.thing} {aim.doing} {aim.contest} {aim.rung} {aim.next} {aim.place} {aim.person} {aim.round}, with {N} {Ns}
# {friend} {parent} {partner} {mentor} {rival}. No sentence starts with an {aim.*} slot (the field's words are lower case).
# per_year is 0 throughout: the Engine sends shape moments for a held aim.
# Knowledge moments open to under-12s (age from 9 or 10) are school-shaped: no money gains, no nights out, no romance.
# Career moments start at 15.

# ================================================================ KNOWLEDGE

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- knowledge: practice, low rungs (cycle s1)

== the long evening with {aim.thing}
tier: life event
shape: knowledge
kind: practice
rungs: 0 1
fork:
stages: child juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 9-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: joy
life: learning, interests
horizon: week
roles: friend, parent, mentor
earth: an ordinary evening of {aim.doing}, the slow kind that adds up over a year
tribal: an evening of {aim.doing} at the edge of the camp, the kind the old ones say adds up
magic: an evening of {aim.doing} in the tower's reading room, the kind the masters say adds up
scene: {N} has been {aim.doing} since supper, and one small piece of it will not come clear. Nobody is making {N} do it; it is simply what holds {Ns} attention this week.
scene tribal: The fire is low and the others are asleep, and {N} is still turning over {aim.thing} the way {mentor} showed. One small part of it will not come clear.
scene magic: The reading room is empty but for {N} and one lamp, and one small part of {aim.thing} still will not come clear.
- W | keep the same hour every evening, whatever else is on | v: conformity, achievement | aim: work | foot: means time-.04 | chance: 85
- U | write down exactly what does not make sense, and start from there | v: self-direction | aim: work | foot: lesson naming the muddle helps | chance: 75
- B | set out to know more of it than anyone around by spring | v: achievement, power | aim: work | foot: person rival | chance: 65
- R | chase the part that is most exciting tonight, and leave the rest | v: stimulation | aim: work | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 70
- G | put it down early and come back to it fresh tomorrow | v: security | aim: ease | foot: means health+.03 | chance: 90
- W>U | ask a teacher to set a little extra each week | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: work | foot: person teacher | chance: 80
- U>B | look up the hardest question on it, and try it alone | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 60
- B>R | make it a race with a friend: who gets further by the weekend | v: achievement, stimulation | aim: work | foot: person friend | chance: 75
- R>G | go out and look for where it turns up in ordinary life | v: stimulation, universalism | aim: work | foot: lesson it turns up everywhere once seen | chance: 75
- G>W | do it beside {parent} at the kitchen table, at an easy pace | v: tradition, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 90
works: The stuck piece gives way all at once, and {N} goes to bed with it still turning over.
works: Nothing dramatic happens, but by the end of the month {N} notices how much more of it makes sense.
fails: The evening slips away and the hard part is exactly as hard as before.
fails: {N} gets halfway, loses the thread, and has to start again next week.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- knowledge: practice, high rungs (cycle s2)

== the slow hours behind every answer
tier: life event
shape: knowledge
kind: practice
rungs: 2 3 4
fork:
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: learning, work
horizon: week
roles: colleague, mentor, rival, elder
earth: the long unglamorous hours of {aim.doing} that the people who come to {N} never see
tribal: the long hours of {aim.doing} away from the fire, the part the young ones never see
magic: the long hours of {aim.doing} in the tower archive, the part the petitioners never see
scene: People come to {N} now for what {N} knows, and every answer is paid for in hours like these: alone at {aim.place}, checking, going back, getting one thing right. More people are asking this year, and there is less time to keep up.
scene tribal: The band comes to {N} with its questions now, and every answer is paid for in hours like these, going back over {aim.thing} until it holds.
scene magic: Petitioners climb the stair to ask {N} things now, and every answer is paid for in hours like these among the archive's shelves.
- W | set aside two fixed mornings a week and guard them from everyone | v: conformity, achievement | aim: work | foot: means time-.05 | chance: 80
- U | go back and check what everyone in the field now takes for granted | v: self-direction, universalism | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 65
- B | keep up only with the work that stays a step ahead of the others | v: power, achievement | aim: work | foot: person rival | chance: 70
- R | follow the strange new thread nobody else has noticed yet | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: work | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 55
- G | cut the hours back to what still feels good, and let the rest wait | v: security, hedonism | aim: ease | foot: means health+.04 | chance: 90
- W>B | join the committee that sets the standard, so the hours count for more | v: conformity, power | aim: work | foot: place rule.counsel | chance: 60
- B>G | take on a younger helper for the checking, and keep the hardest part | v: power, security | aim: work | foot: person colleague | chance: 70
- G>U | sit with an older hand who has done this forty years, and compare notes | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: work | foot: person elder | chance: 80
- U>R | write up what is known so far, rough as it is, and show it | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: work | foot: lesson unfinished work still teaches | chance: 60
- R>W | take a month away, and come back steady for those who rely on the work | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: ease | foot: means freedom+.04 | chance: 85
works: An hour of checking turns up something everyone has been getting slightly wrong, and {N} is the first to see it.
works: The answers come easier this year, because the slow hours are underneath them.
fails: The hours go in and nothing new comes out of them; it is a dry season.
fails: {N} keeps up, just, and is too tired at the end of each week to enjoy any of it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- knowledge: contest, low rungs (cycle s1)

== the first test of what {N} knows
tier: life event
shape: knowledge
kind: contest
rungs: 0 1
fork:
stages: child juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 9-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: learning, school
horizon: week
roles: teacher, friend, rival
earth: {aim.contest}, the first time what {N} knows is checked by someone else
tribal: the day the old ones ask {N} to show what has been learned, in front of the others
magic: the apprentices' trial in the lower hall, set by a master who does not smile
scene: On Thursday there is {aim.contest} at {aim.place}, and for the first time what {N} knows will be checked by someone who does not know {N} at all. There are four days left to get ready, or to decide not to.
scene tribal: Before the next moon the old ones will ask {N} to show what has been learned of {aim.thing}, in front of everyone.
scene magic: The master of the lower hall has set the apprentices' trial for the end of the week, and {Ns} name is on the list.
- W | revise what was set, in the order it was set | v: conformity, security | aim: try | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 80
- U | work out what they are likely to ask, and practise exactly that | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: try | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- B | go in to beat the best of the others, not just to pass | v: achievement, power | aim: try | foot: person rival | chance: 60
- R | go in cold and trust what is already there | v: stimulation, self-direction | aim: try | foot: lesson nerves fade once it starts | chance: 50
- G | ask to sit it another time, when it feels less rushed | v: security | aim: skip | foot: means health+.03 | chance: 90
- W>U | ask a teacher what a good answer looks like, and practise one | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: try | foot: person teacher | chance: 80
- U>B | quiz each other with someone from the group until one cracks | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: try | foot: person friend | chance: 75
- B>R | leave it: a test this small is not worth the fuss | v: power, stimulation | aim: skip | foot: lesson not every test counts | chance: 85
- R>G | go along with {friend} for the company, and see what happens | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: try | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 75
- G>W | stay home to help {parent}, and sit the next one instead | v: benevolence, conformity | aim: skip | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 85
works: {N} comes out lighter than {N} went in, and the result, when it comes, says {N} knew it.
works: Two questions are hard and the rest are kind, and that is enough.
fails: The questions land on the one part {N} skipped.
fails: {N} knew it all last night and only half of it in the morning.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- knowledge: contest, high rungs (cycle s2)

== standing up to be questioned
tier: life event
shape: knowledge
kind: contest
rungs: 2 3 4
fork:
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: learning, work, publiclife
horizon: months
roles: colleague, rival, mentor
earth: {aim.contest} before people who know the subject, where {N} must stand behind every claim
tribal: a gathering of the bands, where {N} must answer the old ones of other camps in front of everyone
magic: a disputation before the masters of three towers, where every claim is defended aloud
scene: Next month {N} is asked to face {aim.contest} at {aim.place}, before people who know {aim.thing} as well as {N} does and are not there to be kind. Saying no now would be noticed; saying yes means the weeks between belong to it.
scene tribal: When the bands meet at the river, the old ones of the other camps want to hear what {N} knows of {aim.thing}, and to argue with it.
scene magic: The masters of three towers will sit at the disputation, and {Ns} claims are the ones on the table.
- W | accept, and prepare by the standards the others will judge by | v: conformity, achievement | aim: try | foot: means time-.06 | chance: 70
- U | accept, and prepare for the hardest question anyone in the room could ask | v: self-direction | aim: try | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 60
- B | accept, and go in to change the room's mind | v: power, achievement | aim: try | foot: person rival | chance: 55
- R | accept, and speak without notes, as it comes | v: stimulation | aim: try | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 45
- G | decline politely: this season belongs to other things | v: security, benevolence | aim: skip | foot: mark turned down a chance | chance: 90
- W>B | accept, and bring along the colleagues who stand behind the work | v: conformity, power | aim: try | foot: person colleague | chance: 65
- B>G | send a younger one in your place, and coach them for it | v: power, benevolence | aim: skip | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 80
- G>U | go, answer plainly, and listen more than talk | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: try | foot: person mentor | chance: 70
- U>R | turn it down, and spend the month on the question itself | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: skip | foot: lesson the work outlasts the stage | chance: 85
- R>W | say yes, and make it a day the young ones in the field remember | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: try | foot: place gather.great | chance: 55
works: The hardest question comes, and {N} has an answer, and the room goes quiet in the good way.
works: {N} is pushed hard on one point and gives ground on it honestly, and that is what people remember.
fails: One question finds the soft place in what {N} knows, and everybody sees it.
fails: It goes well enough, and changes nobody's mind.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- knowledge: mentor (cycle s1)

== the one who has done it before
tier: life event
shape: knowledge
kind: mentor
rungs: 0 1 2
fork:
stages: child juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 10-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: joy
life: learning, mentor
horizon: months
roles: mentor, teacher, friend
earth: someone who has known {aim.thing} for decades notices how {N} goes about it
tribal: an old one of the band watches {N} at it, and says nothing for a long while
magic: a master from the upper tower stops on the stair to watch {N} work
scene: For a few weeks {aim.person} has watched {N} at {aim.place}, and today says it: there is a better way to go about {aim.thing}, and it can be shown, if {N} wants. It would mean being told, every week, where {N} is wrong.
scene tribal: For days the old one has watched {N} at {aim.thing}, and today says it at last: there is a better way, and it can be shown, if {N} will hear where {N} is wrong.
scene magic: The master on the stair has watched {N} for a week, and today offers it: one hour a week, and the truth about every mistake.
- W | accept, and turn up at the agreed hour every week | v: conformity, tradition | aim: work | foot: door kept your word | chance: 85
- U | accept, and come with a list of questions each time | v: self-direction | aim: work | foot: person mentor | chance: 80
- B | accept, and learn everything they know as fast as possible | v: achievement, power | aim: work | foot: person mentor | chance: 70
- R | thank them, and keep doing it your own way | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: ease | foot: mark turned down a chance | chance: 80
- G | ask whether {friend} can come along too | v: benevolence | aim: work | foot: person friend | chance: 80
- W>U | accept, on condition they mark everything strictly | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: work | foot: means time-.04 | chance: 75
- U>B | ask them for hard tests, aimed where the work is weakest | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: try | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 65
- B>R | take the one tip that matters most and run with it alone | v: achievement, stimulation | aim: try | foot: lesson one good tip goes far | chance: 60
- R>G | ask to watch them at their own work instead of being taught | v: stimulation, tradition | aim: work | foot: person mentor | chance: 75
- G>W | say not yet: there is enough on just now, perhaps after the summer | v: security, conformity | aim: ease | foot: means time+.03 | chance: 85
works: The first hour is humbling, the second is better, and by the fifth {N} can feel the difference.
works: It turns out that {aim.person} is patient and {N} is quick, and the hour is the best of the week.
fails: The help is real but the timing is wrong, and the weekly hour falls away by spring.
fails: {N} and the old hand rub each other the wrong way, and it ends politely after a month.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- knowledge: rival (cycle s2)

== the other one who knows
tier: life event
shape: knowledge
kind: rival
rungs: 1 2 3
fork:
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: learning, conflict
horizon: months
roles: rival, colleague, elder, friend
earth: someone else in the same field, as good as {N} or better, and in all the same rooms
tribal: another of the band who also knows {aim.thing}, and whom the others also ask
magic: another apprentice of the same master, cleverer by half and never tired
scene: {rival} knows {aim.thing} as well as {N} does, maybe better, and people have started asking which of the two is right. This week the two of them disagree out loud, at {aim.place}, in front of others.
scene tribal: {rival} also knows {aim.thing}, and this time the band has heard two answers to the same question and is waiting to see which holds.
scene magic: {rival} has the master's ear as well, and today the two of them gave the master opposite answers.
- W | agree on what would settle it, and abide by the result | v: conformity, universalism | aim: try | foot: person rival | chance: 70
- U | go away and check, properly, which answer is right | v: self-direction | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- B | make sure the people who matter hear your side first | v: power | aim: try | foot: person patron | chance: 55
- R | argue it out there and then, as loudly as it takes | v: stimulation | aim: try | foot: person rival | chance: 50
- G | let it go: there is room for two who know it | v: benevolence, security | aim: ease | foot: person friend | chance: 80
- W>B | ask a respected third person to judge between the two answers | v: conformity, power | aim: try | foot: person elder | chance: 65
- B>G | quietly win over the people the rival depends on | v: power, security | aim: try | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 55
- G>U | ask the rival over, and work through it together | v: benevolence, self-direction | aim: work | foot: person colleague | chance: 70
- U>R | take the rival's best point and build something new on it | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: work | foot: lesson a rival sharpens the work | chance: 65
- R>W | stop arguing and challenge them to a fair test in public | v: stimulation, conformity | aim: try | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 55
works: The argument sends {N} back to the work, and what {N} finds settles it.
works: {N} and {rival} end the week still disagreeing, and both a little sharper for it.
fails: Being right turns out to matter less than being liked, and {rival} is better liked.
fails: The quarrel spreads, and people who do not know the subject start picking sides.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- knowledge: setback (cycle s1)

== the answer that was wrong
tier: life event
shape: knowledge
kind: setback
rungs: any
fork:
stages: child juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 10-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: trouble
life: learning, inner
horizon: weeks
roles: mentor, teacher, friend, rival
earth: a mistake made in front of others: a bad mark, a wrong answer given with confidence, or a piece of work turned down
tribal: a wrong word about {aim.thing} given to the band, and the trouble it brought before anyone noticed
magic: an error in {Ns} work that the master found, and read aloud to the hall
scene: Something {N} was sure about turned out wrong, and it was not a private mistake: {aim.person} saw it, and so did others. {N} cannot stop going over it, and the next time is already coming.
scene tribal: {N} told the band something about {aim.thing} with certainty, and it was wrong, and the others noticed before {N} did.
scene magic: The master found the error in {Ns} work and read it aloud to the hall, without unkindness and without mercy.
- W | own the mistake openly, and put it right where it was made | v: conformity, benevolence | aim: work | foot: mark owned up | chance: 75
- U | find exactly where the thinking went wrong | v: self-direction | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- B | come back next time so well prepared nobody remembers it | v: achievement, power | aim: work | foot: means time-.04 | chance: 60
- R | let {aim.thing} go: it has stopped being worth the sting | v: stimulation, hedonism | aim: stop | foot: lesson pride heals slower than skill | chance: 85
- G | take a quiet week, then go back to it gently | v: security | aim: work | foot: means health+.03 | chance: 85
- W>U | ask {aim.person} to go through the mistake step by step | v: conformity, self-direction | aim: work | foot: person mentor | chance: 75
- U>B | write down what went wrong, so it never happens the same way twice | v: self-direction, achievement | aim: work | foot: lesson a mistake written down stays small | chance: 70
- B>R | prove them wrong with something bolder | v: power, stimulation | aim: work | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 50
- R>G | walk it off outside, then talk it through with {friend} | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: work | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 80
- G>W | decide this is not the road, and keep the friends it brought | v: tradition, benevolence | aim: stop | foot: person friend | chance: 85
works: The mistake turns out to have been the useful kind, and {N} never makes it again.
works: A week later almost nobody remembers, and {N} has quietly fixed what caused it.
fails: It keeps coming back at odd moments, and {N} goes quiet whenever {aim.thing} comes up.
fails: {N} puts it right, but the people who saw the mistake never see the correction.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- knowledge: plateau, fork go_on (cycle s2)

== the long flat stretch
tier: life event
shape: knowledge
kind: plateau
rungs: 1 2 3
fork: go_on
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
tone: mixed
life: learning, inner
horizon: years
roles: mentor, friend, parent, colleague
earth: a long stretch of {aim.doing} where nothing seems to get better, however much goes in
tribal: a long season where {N} learns nothing new of {aim.thing}, however hard {N} looks
magic: a year in the tower where the next door will not open, however many hours {N} gives
scene: The next step, {aim.next}, feels no closer than it did a year ago. The hours go in and nothing seems to change, and this spring other things want those hours: work, people, rest. {N} has to decide what the hours are for.
scene tribal: A whole season has passed and {N} has learned nothing new of {aim.thing}, and the band needs hands for the move.
scene magic: For a year the next door in the tower has stayed shut, and {Ns} family writes to ask when {N} will come home.
- W | keep the same routine: the steady way has worked so far | v: conformity, security | aim: work | foot: means time-.04 | chance: 70
- U | change the method entirely, and see what that shows | v: self-direction | aim: work | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 60
- B | find out what the ones further on did differently, and copy it | v: achievement, power | aim: work | foot: person colleague | chance: 60
- R | throw out the routine and follow whatever still stirs curiosity | v: stimulation | aim: work | foot: lesson boredom asks for something new | chance: 60
- G | slow to an easy pace for a while, and let it settle | v: security | aim: ease | foot: means health+.04 | chance: 85
- W>B | set a firm test six months from now, and train for that | v: conformity, achievement | aim: work | foot: door kept your word | chance: 65
- B>G | let it go, and put what it taught into something that pays | v: power, security | aim: stop | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 85
- G>U | come back to it only when a real question pulls hard enough | v: tradition, self-direction | aim: ease | foot: lesson questions return when they are ready | chance: 80
- U>R | give it a season off, and try something next to it | v: self-direction, stimulation | aim: later | foot: means freedom+.04 | chance: 80
- R>W | let it go gracefully, and pass the notes to someone just starting | v: stimulation, benevolence | aim: stop | foot: person friend | chance: 85
works: {N} keeps at it, and one ordinary evening the stuck place gives way.
works: The change of pace is what was needed; {aim.thing} looks different from a step back.
fails: The flat stretch goes on, and {N} begins to wonder whether it ever ends.
fails: Nothing moves this year either, though {N} is no longer sure that matters.

